    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64078" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύκειον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], τό</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Lyceum</i>, a gymnasium at Athens, named after
			the neighbouring temple of Apollo <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύκειος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				356
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.1.33
			</span></i>: a resort of Socrates, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				2a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				271a
			</span></i>; here Aristotle used to discourse, whence his disciples were
			called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύκειοι Περιπατητικοί</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Elias
				<u>in Cat.</u>
				112.31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύκειον</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύκιον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>.</div>
